  "aiContextParagraph": "The Kartarpur Corridor, which serves as a visa-free border crossing between India and Pakistan, has been subject to ongoing security assessments by the Indian government. Home Minister Amit Shah recently addressed the status of the corridor, emphasizing that the decision to facilitate its reopening depends on the successful resolution of national security considerations. This announcement aligns with broader security discussions led by the Ministry of Home Affairs, which oversees border management and counter-terrorism measures. While authorities maintain that the crossing remains a significant pilgrimage route, the government continues to prioritize safety and oversight protocols. The status of the corridor is reviewed periodically in conjunction with domestic and regional security assessments to ensure that all operational procedures meet current requirements before resuming transit activity for pilgrims.",
